<% content_for :title, "atablefor — book a Lisbon table through your AI assistant (demo)" %>

  <div class="agentbar">
    <span class="tag">🤖 For agents</span>
    <span>Agents &amp; AI assistants — <a href="/.well-known/kiosk.json">learn here</a> how to work with this site.</span>
    <a class="what" href="https://kiosk.tech">(what is this?)</a>
  </div>
  <%= render "header", label: "Reservations board", path: "/reservations" %>

  <!-- ── 0. PROTOCOL-PRIMARY banner: this is a machine endpoint ── -->
  <section class="proto">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="proto-badge">🔌 This site works with Kiosk</span>
      <h1>Point your AI assistant here — it books the table.</h1>
      <p>This is <strong>atablefor</strong> — a restaurant booking aggregator across a handful of Lisbon neighbourhoods (Alfama, Graça, Bairro Alto, Belém, Príncipe Real). AI assistants book here through <strong>Kiosk</strong>. There is <strong>no web booking form and no sign-in to reserve</strong>. An assistant finds this site, makes its own account, and books a table.</p>
      <p class="say">“Book a table for two in Alfama tonight at 8.”</p>
      <p class="no-signin">Say that to your assistant. It reads <a href="/.well-known/kiosk.json">/.well-known/kiosk.json</a>, makes its own account, and books — no login, no app, no card. (Staff sign-in, top right, is only for restaurant staff to manage linked diners.)</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap">

    <!-- ── 1. How an assistant books here ────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="sec">
      <div class="sec-k">🤖 How an assistant books here</div>
      <div class="tryit">
        <h2>Book a table — no human at the keyboard</h2>
        <p>Give the one-line prompt to your AI assistant. Behind the scenes it:</p>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>Finds this site through <code>/.well-known/kiosk.json</code> — no web page, no browser login.</li>
          <li>Makes its own account, signed with a key only it holds.</li>
          <li>Calls <code>availability</code>, then <code>book_table</code> — the reservation is confirmed.</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="note">⚠ Every new assistant account pays a <strong>full-strength proof-of-work toll</strong> to register: one memory-hard puzzle, 9 to 20&nbsp;s on one Apple M3 laptop core. Then the toll comes on every 10th call. You feel first-hand the cost that keeps scalpers out. Every Kiosk demo asks the same toll.</p>
        <div class="linkbox">
          <strong>Link a booking to a real diner account.</strong> A diner signs in at <a href="/users/sign_in">Staff login</a> (demo login below), opens <a href="/kiosk/auth/assistants">Manage&nbsp;assistants</a> and makes a one-time link code. Hand that code to the assistant. It uses the code, and its bookings then appear on the <a href="/reservations">reservations board</a> under that diner's name.
          <div class="cred">Demo login: <code>diego@example.com</code> &nbsp;/&nbsp; <code>atablefor-demo-password</code></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── 2. The live reservations board (the reveal) ───────────────── -->
    <section class="sec">
      <div class="sec-k">📋 Live reservations board — see the booking land</div>
      <%= render "board" %>
    </section>

    <!-- ── 3. About this demo ────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="sec">
      <div class="sec-k">About this demo</div>
      <div class="about">
        <p><strong>atablefor</strong> is a restaurant-booking aggregator (a handful of coined Lisbon restaurants, each with a few finite tables) and the example of <strong>linking an assistant to a diner's account</strong>: a diner signs in and makes a link code, their assistant uses it, and the assistant's bookings show under the diner's name on the board above. <strong>No money changes hands</strong>: a reservation takes no card. Tables are finite: a fully-booked seating is honestly sold out.</p>
        <div class="chips">
          <span class="chip">🔗 Diner↔assistant linking</span>
          <span class="chip">Viewable reservations board</span>
          <span class="chip">No payment</span>
          <span class="chip">Full-strength proof-of-work toll (9–20&nbsp;s, Apple M3 core)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="links">
          <a href="https://github.com/kiosk-hq/kiosk/tree/main/kiosk-demo-atablefor">▶ Source on GitHub</a>
          <a href="https://kiosk.tech">What is Kiosk? →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── 4. Live activity (compact) ────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="sec">
      <div class="sec-k">Live activity</div>
      <div class="stats">
        <div class="stat"><div class="n"><%= @tables_booked %></div><div class="l">Tables booked</div></div>
        <div class="stat"><div class="n"><%= @covers_seated %></div><div class="l">Covers seated</div></div>
        <div class="stat"><div class="n"><%= @reservations.size %></div><div class="l">Upcoming</div></div>
        <div class="stat"><div class="n"><%= @restaurants %></div><div class="l">Restaurants</div></div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>
